. * Does the child have a vaccination card, dates copied off the card, and then
>  a recall quesiton asking the parents if their child was vaccinated.
. * NOTE: Different from 2009 as 2005 has only ONE card (vac02). There is no va
> c02_a (previous card), and the card dates are vac03a-vac03u with no _1/_2 suf
> fix. 
. keep folio ls vac02 vac03a-vac03u vac04a vac04b vac04c vac04d vac04e vac04f v
> ac04g vac04h

. rename vac02 has_vaccination_card

. * IMPORTANT NOTE: Skip pattern, VAC04 is asked ONLY when no card is seen. If 
> a card is seen VAC02 = 1 the interviewer copies the dates into VAC03 and skip
> s VAC04.
. 
. * This generates a categorical variable that denotes if 1 = you had a card, 2
>  = a previous card, or 3 = a recall.
. * Note: No previous card in 2005, so there is no card_src = 2 line. We keep t
> he same numbering as 2009 (1 = card, 3 = recall)
. gen byte card_src = 1 if has_vaccination_card == 1
(6,725 missing values generated)

. replace card_src = 3 if inlist(has_vaccination_card, 2, 3)
(5,117 real changes made)

. 
. * Writing a loop to check if there is a date corresponding with if the child 
> is vaccinated. So r_ = 1 if the card shows the dose was given a real date, or
>  "44" = given but date not recorded, and 0 if the box is blank or "45". 45 me
> ans not vaccinateed because too young
. foreach v of varlist vac03a-vac03u {
  2.     gen byte r_`v' = (trim(`v') != "" & substr(trim(`v'), 1, 2) != "45")
  3. }

. 
