. * This code converts the pid_link to a string and generates a variable to den
> ote the wave 2005. I think already a string so can delete this line but it do
> esn't hurt anything.
. capture confirm string variable pid_link

. if _rc tostring pid_link, replace format(%010.0f)

. gen wave = 2005

. gen pid_link_canonical = pid_link

. 
. * We open the 2002 do file to carry over the birth-related variables that we 
> list.
. * Drop any individuals that are missing but it should be zero, we also only k
> eep 1 individual
. * We add _02 ending so the merge doesn't clash and we can check 
. * Then we merge, attaches the 2002 values to each 2005 child with the same ID
> . Note we only keep the master since we don't want to double count the wave 2
> 002 (note that's only part of the reason but a good one)
. * For each of these six variables, if the child has a 2002 value, use it, ove
> rwriting the 2005 value. If there's no 2002 value, the 2005 one stays. 2002 l
> inked pregnancies to children by exact line number, and these traits can't ch
> ange after birth, so 2002 is the more reliable source
. preserve

.     use pid_link_canonical birth_order oldest_child birth_weight_kg delivered
> _home predominant_breastfed still_breastfed iron_pregnancy premature using "$
> clean_mxfls/mxfls_2002_master.dta", clear

